    {
      "id": "claim_19d1a73d281b4afa8a9e942a300577d3",
      "statement": "The circular block bootstrap is the distribution-free alternative to the closed-form Lo (2002) standard error, chosen because the naive i.i.d. bootstrap destroys the autocorrelation and volatility clustering of financial returns; it wraps the series into a circle and resamples contiguous blocks whose length should grow with the autocorrelation horizon.",
      "evidence": [
        {
